  "onboardingSlide1Title": "Verify who is on the line.",
  "@onboardingSlide1Title": {"description": "Headline of onboarding slide 1 (what Signet is for)."},

  "onboardingSlide1Body": "Deepfake voice and video can sound like anyone — a family member, a colleague, a source. When someone calls with urgency, asking for money, for help, for access, Signet lets you ask for a rotating 4-word phrase only their real phone can produce. If the words match, you know.",
  "@onboardingSlide1Body": {"description": "Body of onboarding slide 1."},

  "onboardingSlide2Title": "Pair once, in person.",
  "@onboardingSlide2Title": {"description": "Headline of onboarding slide 2 (how pairing works)."},

  "onboardingSlide2Body": "You pair two phones by scanning each other's QR codes while you're together. The shared secret stays on both devices — hardware-backed, offline, no cloud. Nothing to subpoena. Nothing to phish. Nothing to sync to a server that doesn't exist.",
  "@onboardingSlide2Body": {"description": "Body of onboarding slide 2."},

  "onboardingSlide3Title": "Ask for the phrase.",
  "@onboardingSlide3Title": {"description": "Headline of onboarding slide 3 (how to verify a call)."},

  "onboardingSlide3Body": "During the call, open Signet, tap the peer, ask them to read their 4 words. Type what you hear. Green banner = verified, trust the call. Red banner = do not trust it. Hang up and call back on a number you already know.",
  "@onboardingSlide3Body": {"description": "Body of onboarding slide 3."},

